-- title:
--   Full Slice Scalar Marginalize Y
-- statement:
--   **Second-term full-to-evaluated slice comparison with the Schwartz-Zippel loss.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a symmetric strategy with normalized state $\psi$, and let $G^x$ be a strongly self-consistent projective family of degree-$d$ polynomial measurements on slices over $\mathbb{F}_q$. The full-slice quartic average sums the ordered four-factor product over uniform heights and polynomial outcomes, while the evaluated-slice quartic average evaluates the corresponding outcomes at two uniformly sampled ambient points. If the strong self-consistency error is $\zeta$, then
--
--   $$
--   \left|\operatorname{fullSliceABABAvg}(S,G)-\operatorname{evaluatedSliceABABAvg}(S,G)\right|
--   \le 2\frac{md}{q}+4\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   The first term is the two-coordinate Schwartz-Zippel loss and the remaining terms come from the intermediate scalar and tensor comparisons. This is the second scalar transport estimate used by the full-slice commutation lemma.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.fullSlice_scalar_marginalize_y`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
